## What a Product Launch Needs From AV

A product launch is a specific kind of presentation: the room is often lit for photography, guests move around the product before and after the reveal, and the presenter usually wants to walk the floor rather than stand at a lectern. Our [Product Presentation Pack](/packages/product-presentation/) is built around that: a 5000-lumen laser projector stays legible in a lit room instead of a dim conference hall, and a wireless handheld microphone, not a corded one, keeps the presenter free to move.

<InlineCTA />

## Connecting Your Own Devices

Most launches run off the presenter's own laptop, tablet or media player, not ours. We provide the HDMI and USB-C adapters and audio interfaces to connect your equipment to our screen and sound system, so the walkthrough is confirming the connection on arrival, not solving it on the spot.

## What We Provide, and What We Don't

We provide a front projection screen with a stable stand, a 5000-lumen Full HD laser projector, a venue sound system with 2 speakers and a mixing console, and a wireless handheld microphone. We do not provide an LED video wall: this is a projector-and-screen setup, sized for a launch's visuals rather than a broadcast-scale wall.

We also do not provide cameras, a live streaming feed or broadcast equipment. If your launch needs a stage or riser for the reveal itself, that is not part of this package either; our [audio visual rental for gala dinners](/blog/audio-visual-rental-for-gala-dinners/) guide covers the MICE Pack's optional staging for that kind of setup.

